  "decisions": [
    "Keep the three top-level business categories. Use specific use cases for retail, trades, agencies, educators and creators instead of more overlapping filters.",
    "Keep all seven goals and five formats. Do not fill irrelevant cells, such as cart recovery for publishers or forced fullscreen signup.",
    "Do not mistake the two curated cart setups for missing popup recovery: delayed and exit cart playbooks already exist outside the studio.",
    "Prioritise clear SMS expectations, service boundaries and project evidence. Reuse the existing sample-plus-form design for newsletter sampling.",
    "Review dormant designs before making more generic offers, coupons, split signups or newsletter cards.",
    "Freshly review the 92 stale studio approvals before including those setups in a hosted release. Stale is not a claim that a template is broken.",
    "Do not add booking calendars, live cart contents, SKU restock subscriptions, real-time inventory, shipping calculators or conditional entitlement checks as template-only promises. Those need product capability work."
  ],
